I'm stopping here. The evidence supports one candidate fault, and it does not reach users.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "geo",
      "fault_kind": "container_cpu_saturated",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "metric", "sql": "SELECT 'normal' p, ROUND(AVG(value),3) avg_cpu_cores, COUNT(*) n FROM normal_metrics WHERE metric='container.cpu.usage' AND attr_k8s_pod_name='geo-68f8cb558f-jj4hj' UNION ALL SELECT 'abnormal', ROUND(AVG(value),3), COUNT(*) FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE metric='container.cpu.usage' AND attr_k8s_pod_name='geo-68f8cb558f-jj4hj'", "claim": "geo pod container CPU usage rises from about 0.003 cores to about 1.56 cores in the abnormal window."},
        {"kind": "metric", "sql": "SELECT metric, ROUND(AVG(value),0) avg_bytes FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE attr_k8s_pod_name='geo-68f8cb558f-jj4hj' AND metric IN ('container.memory.usage','container.memory.rss') GROUP BY metric", "claim": "geo pod memory usage and RSS are also elevated, about 27 MB and 21 MB, against roughly 18 MB and 15 MB normally."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT 'normal' p, ROUND(approx_quantile(duration,0.5)/1e6,3) p50_ms, ROUND(approx_quantile(duration,0.95)/1e6,3) p95_ms, COUNT(*) n FROM normal_traces WHERE service_name='geo' AND span_name='geo.Geo/Nearby' UNION ALL SELECT 'abnormal', ROUND(approx_quantile(duration,0.5)/1e6,3), ROUND(approx_quantile(duration,0.95)/1e6,3), COUNT(*) FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='geo' AND span_name='geo.Geo/Nearby'", "claim": "geo.Geo/Nearby latency is essentially unchanged (p95 about 0.19 ms to 0.20 ms); the CPU burn did not slow its own requests."}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": []
}
```

Caveat, which the schema could not carry: the geo CPU burn is the only real resource anomaly I found, but I found no evidence that it reached `search`, `frontend`, or any user-facing request. Its span latency, error share and call volume are flat, and no network or restart signals changed. Because propagation is unproven, this root cause should be treated as low-confidence. The mild `frontend /user` and `/reservation` tail increases rest on about 20 requests each and are not attributable to any fault.

